  "method": "OpenStreetMap way 162058026 (building=yes, name SLAC Klystron Gallery); nodes kept verbatim from an Overpass extract, no simplification. The Klystron Gallery is the continuous above-ground structure built directly over the buried linac beam tunnel it powers (SLAC's public-tours page: 'SLAC is home to the historic 2-mile-long klystron gallery above the world’s longest linear particle accelerator.', src:dw-slac-public-tours-klystron-gallery); its own footprint is used here as the accelerator's surface trace, honestly represented as a building feature rather than the buried tunnel itself.",
